    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Since you mentioned the lack of \"noisy\" overtones in the flute, how do those more complex or irregular partials affect the sound in something like a bassoon or an oboe? I've heard people refer to certain acoustic artifacts or \"ghostly\" qualities in woodwinds—does that have a mathematical basis in the harmonic series?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
